  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of symmetric relations defined on the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math> which are not reflexive is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "960",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We know that,</p><p>Total number of relation both symmetric and reflexive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is number of elements in given set,</p><p>Also, total number of symmetric relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></msup></math></p><p>Then number of symmetric relation which are not reflexive will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1024</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>64</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>960</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}